==Finnish==

===Etymology===
An old consonant-stem verb, etymologically identical to {{m|fi|tuntea}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{fi-p|*}}

===Verb===
{{fi-verb}}

# {{lb|fi|obsolete|literary|crosswords}} {{alternative form of|fi|tuntea|nodot=1}} ("to feel"; also "to get to feel", "to experience").
#: ''Olen elämässäni saanut '''tuta''' kaikenlaista, mutta tällaista raakuutta en ole ennen nähnyt.''
#:: I have '''experienced''' a lot during my lifetime, but I have never seen brutality like this.

====Usage notes====
Only used in first infinitive ('''''tuta''''', {{m|fi|tutakseen}}), passive present indicative ({{m|fi|tutaan}}) and rarely in instructive of second active infinitive ({{m|fi|tutaen}}). The passive past participle ({{m|fi|tuttu}}) is in modern usage viewed simply as an adjective meaning "familiar", and the passive present participle ({{m|fi|tuttava}}) as a noun meaning "acquaintance". It is also still common in phrases like ''saada tuta''. All other uses are obsolete.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|to feel}} {{l|fi|tuntea}}
* {{sense|to experience}} {{l|fi|kokea}}

